        {
          "type": "terms",
          "items": [
            [
              "Dot product",
              "Sum of products of matching entries; a scalar."
            ],
            [
              "Cross product",
              "3D vector perpendicular to both."
            ],
            [
              "@",
              "Matrix multiplication."
            ],
            [
              "Inner dimensions",
              "Columns of the first = rows of the second."
            ],
            [
              "Inverse",
              "A⁻¹ with A⁻¹A = I."
            ],
            [
              "np.linalg.solve",
              "Solves AX = B."
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "formulas",
          "title": "Formulas",
          "items": [
            {
              "label": "Dot",
              "latex": "\\mathbf A\\cdot\\mathbf B=\\sum a_ib_i=|A||B|\\cos\\theta"
            },
            {
              "label": "Cross",
              "latex": "\\mathbf A\\times\\mathbf B=[a_2b_3-a_3b_2,\\;a_3b_1-a_1b_3,\\;a_1b_2-a_2b_1]"
            },
            {
              "label": "Shapes",
              "latex": "(m\\times n)(n\\times p)\\to(m\\times p)"
            },
            {
              "label": "Linear system",
              "latex": "AX=B\\;\\Rightarrow\\;X=A^{-1}B"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "warn",
          "md": "- **`*` for matrix multiplication**: use `@`.\n- **Dimension mismatch**: (2×3) @ (2×2) is an error.\n- **Cross product order**: swapping flips the sign.\n- **Singular matrix**: `inv` fails (or gives huge numbers) if rows are multiples of each other.",
          "title": "Classic mistakes"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "exam",
          "md": "Exam 2 was multiple choice, about 40 minutes, no AI tools. Review item: matrix multiplication / dot product.",
          "title": "How Exam 2 tested this"
